## Comparison with Other Tools

| Feature | ClarVar | bcftools | Ensembl VEP |
|---|---|---|---|
| Lightweight (pip install) | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Real VEP annotation | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ |
| gnomAD v4.1 frequencies | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| ClinVar integration | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| CADD / SIFT / PolyPhen | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ |
| Composite priority scoring | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| HTML report with links | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Python API | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ |
| No local DB required | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |

---

## Limitations

- Requires internet access for VEP annotation (use `LocalAnnotator` for offline use)
- Annotation speed is ~3–5 seconds per 200-variant batch due to the Ensembl VEP rate limit; large cohorts benefit from local VEP
- Single-sample VCF files only (multi-sample support planned)
- Structural variants are skipped
- VEP REST API has a rate limit (~15 requests/second); large cohorts benefit from local VEP

---

## Roadmap

**v0.2.0** (current) — Real Ensembl VEP API, gnomAD v4.1, HTML/TSV/JSON reports, 62 passing tests  
**v0.3.0** (planned) — HPO gene filtering, Snakemake wrapper, multi-sample VCF support  
**v0.4.0** (planned) — Local VEP / offline mode, Docker image for HPC  
**v1.0.0** (planned) — Benchmarked against ClinVar gold standard, performance-optimised for large cohorts  

